# Never ship local-development env files to a Vercel build. Vite inlines
# VITE_* variables at build time, so a leaked local .env (pointing at
# http://localhost:4000 for Docker Compose dev) would otherwise get baked
# directly into the production JS bundle — this is what actually happened
# on this project's first deploy before this file existed. Real production
# values belong in the Vercel project's own Environment Variables (see
# `vercel env add`), never in a file carried over from local dev.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
